            "target_entity_type": "Variable",
            "paragraph": "Our climate change forecasting procedure loosely followed the approach described in Hollowed et al. (2009). Future water temperature and salinity projections were gathered from global climate model outputs from the Coupled Model Intercomparison Project 6 (Eyring et al. 2016). We took climate projections from one model, EC-Earth3-CC, based on its accuracy in hindcasting temperatures for North America (Almazroui et al. 2021; Mahony et al. 2022) and availability of monthly average predictions of the desired climate variables (mean near surface air temperature [tas] and surface ocean salinity [sos]) from the automatically quality controlled data hosted by the Climate Data Store (Copernicus Climate Change Service, Climate Data Store (Copernicus 2021)). We selected a set of constant temperature and salinity values from the range of predicted monthly average increases between 2022 and 2049 from two emissions scenarios, SSP2-4.5 and SSP5-8.5 (Eyring et al. 2016).",
